n`` points at the next\n+        element).\n+\n+        Precedence: ``INTERSECT`` binds more tightly than ``UNION`` /\n+        ``EXCEPT``.  ``UNION`` and ``EXCEPT`` are left-associative.\n+\n+        Implementation: flatten the entire linked list into a sequence of\n+        ``(select_plan, op_kind, op_all)`` entries, then fold them with a\n+        two-pass algorithm \u2014 first handle INTERSECT groups from left to right,\n+        then fold the remaining UNION / EXCEPT operations left to right.\n \n         Raises:\n             PlanningError: If the statement cannot be resolved against the\n                 catalog.\n             TableNotFoundError: If it names an unregistered table.\n         \"\"\"\n-        plan = self._compile_select(statement)\n-        operation = statement.set_operation\n-        if operation is None:\n-            return plan\n-        if operation.kind != \"union\":\n-            raise PlanningError(f\"unsupported set operation {operation.kind!r}\")\n-        right = self.compile(operation.statement)\n-        if len(plan.schema) != len(right.schema):\n-            raise PlanningError(\n-                \"UNION requires both sides to produce the same number of columns: \"\n-                f\"{len(plan.schema)} and {len(right.schema)}\"\n-            )\n-        combined: LogicalPlan = Union(plan, right, operation.all)\n-        return combined if operation.all else Distinct(combined)\n+        # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n+        # Step 1: flatten the linked list.\n+        # Each element: (plan, op_kind_leading_to_next, op_all_flag).\n+        # The last element has op_kind=None.\n+        # ----------------------------------------------------------------\n+        stmts: List[Tuple[Optional[str], bool, SelectStatement]] = []\n+        cur: Optional[SelectStatement] = statement\n+        while cur is not None:\n+            op = cur.set_operation\n+            # Strip the set_operation from the